<title>FRANCE: French grain delegation on routine trip to China.</title>
<headline>French grain delegation on routine trip to China.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A team of French grain industry leaders is in China this week for routine talks organised through France-China Cereals, a venture promoting French wheat sales to China, industry officals said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The delegation includes the director general of France's ONIC cereals office, Alain Moulinier, and the director general of France's AGPB wheat growers' association, Georges Malpel.</p>
<p>It also includes representatives from French trading firms Soufflet, Sigma and Champagne Cereales.</p>
<p>The trip is mainly to discuss grain quality, officials said.</p>
<p>As a result of the visit, ONIC's key monthly supply/demand statistics will be published on Wednesday April 16, instead of on the second Wednesday of the month as normal, an ONIC official said.</p>
<p>--Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
